# The origin a deployment answers at, and the only file that holds it. Compose
# hands this to the containers (`env_file` in docker-compose.yml) and nothing
# else reads it: a checkout's `.env` is its own dev environment, and the two
# cannot be one file — this box is both a deploy target and a checkout, so one
# key holding both values is a dev server serving the deployed origin or a
# deployment serving loopback.
#
# The name is the other half of that: vite and bun load `.env`, `.env.local` and
# `.env.<mode>`, and never a name shaped like this one, so no dev run can pick
# a deployed origin up whatever mode it is in.
#
# Origins only, and that is a contract rather than a habit: every key here is
# one a checkout's env may then name nowhere but this machine, so a deployment
# variable that is not an origin — a DSN, a token, a feature flag — belongs in
# docker-compose.yml under the service that reads it, and scripts/origins.ts
# refuses this file if one lands here.
#
# No secrets here either — the same public name infra/nginx/project-template.conf
# serves, which is what scripts/env-wiring.test.ts holds it to. scripts/preview.sh
# writes a file of this shape for the preview stack, which is why compose takes
# the name from ORIGINS_ENV rather than spelling this one twice.
SITE_URL=https://project-template.example.com
